  (a) real-ingest — measures heavy metals in ANY in-scope consumer-product or supply-chain matrix with extractable concentration data. In-scope is food AND non-food: food/beverage, infant food, personal care, feminine care (tampons/pads), cosmetics, cleaning/household products, toys & children's durables, textiles/apparel, pet food/products, dietary supplements, research chemicals/peptides/SARMs, packaging & food-contact materials, and supply-chain inputs tied to a product. "Not food" is NEVER a skip reason — HMTc certifies many non-food categories. ALSO real-ingest: MITIGATION / REMEDIATION interventions — a peptide, plant, biochar, amendment, or process that REMOVES or REDUCES heavy metals (phytoremediation, bioremediation, chelation, sequestration, agronomic/processing levers). "Not occurrence" is NOT a skip. Route these to the wiki/mitigation/ dimension and the metal pages, leave products/ingredients EMPTY (unless the intervention targets a specific crop/product) so their spiked-solution/soil numbers never enter occurrence thresholds. See docs/conventions.md "Ingest scope" and existing pages like urosevic2024-salix-phytoremediation.
